THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS

FreeWilly itself is Apache-2.0 and free at any headcount. The engine it installs is
upstream software under its own terms, listed below. Those files are not redistributed
here: they are downloaded from their official locations at install time, against the
versions and digests this build pins.


Alpine Linux minirootfs
  version  3.24.1
  licence  multiple; see the packages inside it
  source   https://dl-cdn.alpinelinux.org/alpine/v3.24/releases/x86_64/alpine-minirootfs-3.24.1-x86_64.tar.gz
  A base filesystem made of separately licensed packages: musl (MIT), BusyBox and
  apk-tools (GPL-2.0-only) and others. Each package records its own licence under
  /usr/share/licenses inside the installed distribution.

Docker Engine (Moby) static binaries for Linux
  version  29.7.2
  licence  Apache-2.0
  source   https://download.docker.com/linux/static/stable/x86_64/docker-29.7.2.tgz
  dockerd, containerd, runc, ctr and docker-proxy are Apache-2.0. The archive also
  carries docker-init, which is tini, under MIT.

Docker CLI for Windows
  version  29.7.2
  licence  Apache-2.0
  source   https://download.docker.com/win/static/stable/x86_64/docker-29.7.2.zip
  The docker command this project installs and puts on PATH.

Docker Compose CLI plugin for Windows
  version  5.4.0
  licence  Apache-2.0
  source   https://github.com/docker/compose/releases/download/v5.4.0/docker-compose-windows-x86_64.exe
  A separate upstream release with its own version, because the Windows CLI archive does
  not carry it. Installed as a CLI plugin under this install's own config directory
